# part 1: the Silica sentinel S, the Silica edge E and the Rust edge A; every clock is 1500
J1 E joined through S, then A joined through S: A holds E in its edge store and S in its sentinel store
H1 A's tick: A shuffled its edge store with E, its own entry first at age 0; E holds A at age 0
H2 E's tick: E shuffled its edge store with A; A answered and holds E at age 0
H3 S's tick: S shuffled its edge store with A
H4 A's tick of its sentinel store: A shuffled with S and holds S at age 0 again
H5 a sample of A's edge store by another peer -> reply sample_reply entries=[0:b19edad2958934e1] store=tempus_edge peer=9200d2990c3e9eb7 typ=tempus_edge
# refusals: each step is done to the Silica node E and to the Rust node A, and their audit lines are compared
R1 an expired token -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: admission_refused peer=958cff49930885d2 the token has expired
R2 a token that is not valid yet -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: admission_refused peer=958cff49930885d2 the token is not valid yet
R3 a token another key signed -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: admission_refused peer=958cff49930885d2 the signature does not verify
R4 a token under the old kid -> the peer saw key_rotated at=challenge; both nodes: key_rotated peer=958cff49930885d2 the peer's token is under another kid; it was told the current one
R5 a token whose sub is another key -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: admission_refused peer=958cff49930885d2 sub is not the peer's key
R6 somebody else's advert -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: binding_refused peer=cb133950f3232872 the advert's pub is not the key of the peer's TLS certificate
R7 an advert whose id is not the hash of its pub -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: admission_refused peer=cb133950f3232872 id is not the SHA-512 of pub
R8 a sentinel token under a certificate that is not whitelisted -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: whitelist_reject peer=958cff49930885d2 a tempus_bridge or tempus_sentinel token under a certificate that is not in the tempus whitelist
R9 a whitelisted certificate with an edge token -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: whitelist_reject peer=9e1113ab416dc197 a certificate of the tempus whitelist with a token whose typ is not tempus_bridge or tempus_sentinel
R10 a proof by another key -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: pop_failed peer=958cff49930885d2 the proof of possession does not verify
R11 a proof over another nonce -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: pop_failed peer=958cff49930885d2 the proof of possession does not verify
R12 a proof of 63 bytes -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: pop_failed peer=958cff49930885d2 sig is not 64 bytes
R13 no proof: the request comes where it was due -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: pop_failed peer=958cff49930885d2 a response was expected
R14 a first frame that is no advert -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: protocol_error peer=- the first frame is not an advert
R15 a second advert where the challenge was due -> the peer saw closed at=response; both nodes: protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 a challenge was expected
R16 a first frame above the frame ceiling -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: protocol_error peer=- frame refused before decoding: too_large
R17 a request above the frame ceiling -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 frame refused before decoding: too_large
R18 a sample of more than the shuffle length -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 n is not 1 to the shuffle length
R19 a sample of more than the store's shuffle length -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 n is not 1 to the shuffle length
R20 a sample with an unknown key -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 unknown_field
R21 a sample of a store that is no peer type -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 store is not a peer type
R22 a shuffle of more entries than the shuffle length -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 more entries than the shuffle length
R23 a shuffle with an age above 65535 -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 age is not 0 to 65535
R24 a shuffle with an entry another key signed, beside a good one -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | entry_refused peer=958cff49930885d2 entry 1: the signature does not verify
R25 a shuffle of the sentinel store with an edge's entry -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | entry_refused peer=958cff49930885d2 entry 0: typ is not the store's type
R26 a shuffle of the bridge store with more entries than that store's shuffle length -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | shuffle_refused peer=- the store refused the frame
R27 a request that is no term -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 not a request: bad_version
R28 a reply frame where a request was due -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 not a request: unknown kind
R29 a call: neither node is a bridge -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | request_refused peer=958cff49930885d2 call and cast are served by a bridge only
R30 a cast: neither node is a bridge -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | request_refused peer=958cff49930885d2 call and cast are served by a bridge only
R31 a token under the old kid that has also expired -> the peer saw key_rotated at=challenge; both nodes: key_rotated peer=958cff49930885d2 the peer's token is under another kid; it was told the current one
R32 a token that is not a token: its last byte is cut off -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: admission_refused peer=958cff49930885d2 truncated
R33 an advert whose id is 63 bytes -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: protocol_error peer=- id is not 64 bytes
R34 an advert of version 2 -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: protocol_error peer=- ver is not 1
R35 a bridge token under a certificate that is not whitelisted -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: whitelist_reject peer=958cff49930885d2 a tempus_bridge or tempus_sentinel token under a certificate that is not in the tempus whitelist
R36 a sample where the challenge was due -> the peer saw closed at=response; both nodes: protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 a challenge was expected
R37 a sample of 0 -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 n is not 1 to the shuffle length
R38 a shuffle with an entry whose token has expired -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | entry_refused peer=958cff49930885d2 entry 0: the token has expired
R39 a shuffle of the edge store with an entry of a bridge -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | entry_refused peer=958cff49930885d2 entry 0: typ is not the store's type
R40 a frame of no kind -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 not a request: unknown kind
R41 a frame whose t is an atom of the rejection list -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 not a request: unknown kind
R42 a call that names a module and a function the node holds no atom for -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 not a request: unknown_atom
R43 a sample with a value that is an atom of TRUST's results -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 store is not a peer type
R44 a request with a byte after it -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 not a request: trailing_bytes
R45 a request that is not a map -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 not a request: bad_tag
R46 the peer stays silent where its challenge was due, past the node's time bound -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: timeout peer=958cff49930885d2 stage challenge
R47 the peer closes after its advert -> the peer saw closed at=challenge; both nodes: closed_by_peer peer=(any) stage (any)
R48 the peer stays silent where its request was due, past the node's time bound -> the peer saw closed at=request; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | timeout peer=958cff49930885d2 stage request
R49 the peer stays silent where its proof was due, past the node's time bound -> the peer saw closed at=response; both nodes: timeout peer=958cff49930885d2 stage response
R50 TLS: another ALPN protocol -> the peer saw tls_failed at=tls; both nodes: alpn_mismatch peer=- the peer did not agree on ALPN tempus/1, as server
R51 TLS: no certificate -> the peer saw tls_failed at=tls; both nodes: tls_verify_failed peer=- the peer presented no certificate, as server
R52 TLS: a P-256 certificate -> the peer saw closed at=advert; both nodes: tempus_cert_key peer=- the peer certificate's key is not Ed25519, as server
R53 TLS: version 1.2 only -> the peer saw tls_failed at=tls; both nodes: tls_handshake_failed peer=- the TLS 1.3 handshake failed (alert, version, group, suite or signature outside the tempus/1 profile), as server
R54 a third connection while two are held open (inflight_max is 2) -> the peer saw closed at=advert; both nodes: inflight_refused peer=- more accepted connections than inflight_max: closed at once
# the clock of A: clock_back hold, clock_fail continue
C1 A's clock reads 1505: a token that ends at 1500 is inside the skew of 10 -> reply
C2 the clock goes back to 1490 and A holds 1510: the same token has expired by the held time -> closed
C3 a reading fails: A goes on with its last reading and still serves -> reply
C4 the next reading, 1495, is still behind: the hold is said once more; at 1510 the hold ends
C5 A's clock reads 3050: E's entry, whose token ended at 3000, left A's view; the view is empty, so A asked S again, and refused S's token, which has ended too
C6 A's clock reads 4100, past its own token: ticking stopped; A still listens, and a peer's own check refuses A's advert -> refused
C7 the application passes a new token: A ticks again and a peer admits it -> reply
# part 2, node T: clock_back stop with the limit 60, clock_fail pause; no sentinel answers it
T1 a reading fails: T waits for its clock; a connection is closed at once after its handshake -> closed at=advert
T2 the join's retry falls due during the wait and dials nobody; when the clock is read again it is dialed at once
T3 a step back of 51 s, inside the limit of 60: followed
T4 a step back of 70 s, above the limit: T has stopped; a connection is closed at once -> closed at=advert
T5 a later good reading, the join's retry and a tick change nothing: T stays stopped -> closed at=advert
# part 2, node U: its clock cannot be read at its start
U1 no reading at the start: U has not begun and does not listen -> unreachable
U2 the first reading that succeeds: U listens and serves -> reply
# part 3: the Rust node R (tempus-node-example, no test program) and the Silica node P; both read the machine's clock
M1 P's first try found nobody; R started; P's retry joined through R
M2 R's own timer ticked its edge store: R shuffled with P, and P answered
M3 a sample of R's edge store by another peer, which reads the machine's clock too -> reply sample_reply entries=[0:1fae2ad7f75a0ded] store=tempus_edge peer=9e1113ab416dc197 typ=tempus_sentinel
M4 a test-only tick frame: to a node that is no test program a frame of no kind -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 not a request: unknown_atom
M5 a test-only clock frame: to a node that is no test program a frame of no kind -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 not a request: unknown_atom
M6 a test-only clock frame with two readings: to a node that is no test program a frame of no kind -> the peer saw closed at=reply; both nodes: admitted peer=958cff49930885d2 tempus_edge, token and proof of possession | protocol_error peer=958cff49930885d2 not a request: unknown_atom
